    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Check NWS updates here At 902 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm over Bear Creek Summit, or 11 miles east of Weiser, moving northeast at 25 mph. HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph and pea size hail. SOURCE...Radar indicated. IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured objects. Areas of blowing dust possible. Minor damage to outdoor objects is possible. This strong thunderstorm will be near... Bear Creek Summit and Star Butte around 910 PM MDT. Crane Creek Reservoir around 920 PM MDT.",
